  "subdivision_of_building": "A portion of the roof",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "The proposal is to deliver a low- or zero-carbon heating system, designed around a renewable Air Source Heat Pump (ASHP) solution as well as 68no. Solar Panels at roof level. \n\nProposal is to fit 4no. 20kW Panasonic Air Source Heat Pumps mounted at roof level above the existing plant room on a bespoke galvanised steel support frame with handrail and lockable gate. The existing boiler flues to be removed and any redundant penetration in the roof felt are to be made good.\nFurthermore, the existing heat emitters are no longer suitable for retention or reuse, therefore new radiators are to be installed with new pipework is to be provided in areas that are currently unheated.\n\nSolar panels are proposed to be installed at roof level on the two pitched roofs located on opposite sides of the building, as well as on the flat roofs positioned centrally, as shown on the proposed roof plan. \n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The plant equipment hereby permitted shall only operate between the daytime hours of 07:00 and 23:00 each day, as outlined in the Noise Impact Assessment prepared by Nova Acoustics, dated 16 April 2026. \r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the plant equipment during night hours, in accordance with policy D14 of the London Plan 2021 policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The rating level of the noise from the plant hereby permitted shall be at least 5dBA lower than the existing background noise level at any given time of operation. The noise levels shall be measured or predicted 1m externally to any window at the nearest residential façade. Measurements and assessment shall be made according to British Standard 4142:2014.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D14 of the London Plan 2021 policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The works shall be carried out and maintained in accordance with the deposited Reasonable Exception Statement compliant with Policy D12(A).\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan 2021."
  ],
